        // (zero address can still be pranked, but avoid constraining too much). No tight assumptions.
        // Ensure caller is a distinct EOA-ish address (fuzzer supplies EOAs only) — no helper contracts needed.

        // The contract has an onlyOwner modifier on setApprovedLogger. We must call as the owner.
        // By default C._contractOwner is zero (private) — but we cannot access it. To make the call succeed
        // we need to be the owner. The simplest way is to call setApprovedLogger from the same address that created C.
        // setUp() used address(this) (test contract) to deploy C, so address(this) is the owner. We'll impersonate address(this).
        // However the fuzzed 'caller' should be the caller that the reference and mutant compare against (msg.sender inside call).
        // To achieve this, we will have the owner (address(this)) call a small forwarding helper that performs the external call
        // to c.setApprovedLogger with tx.origin/computed msg.sender equal to the fuzzed 'caller'. But msg.sender inside C will be
        // the immediate caller (the helper). Therefore we instead use the following approach:
        // - We will have the test contract (the owner) perform the call to c.setApprovedLogger. The msg.sender seen by C will be address(this).
        // - The property we check is: c.approvedLoggers(target) equals status after owner invoked setApprovedLogger on behalf of 'caller' parameter.
        // To make the fuzzed 'caller' actually differ from the caller used at the EVM level (address(this)), we must pass 'target' as the intended key.
        // The mutant bug uses msg.sender as mapping key instead of the provided target. Thus the only relevant differing addresses are where caller != target.
        // Because only the owner can call setApprovedLogger, we will keep owner as the executor (address(this)). The fuzzer still provides 'target' and 'status'.
        // This captures the difference: reference will set approvedLoggers[target] == status, mutant will set approvedLoggers[address(this)] == status.

        // Call as owner (address(this)) — no vm.prank necessary because test contract is the deployer/owner.
        // Wide domain: allow target to be any address (including address(this) occasionally). The property must hold for ALL inputs.

        // Execute
        c.setApprovedLogger(target, status);

        // Single assertion: approvedLoggers(target) must equal status. This is true for the reference for all inputs.
        // The mutant that writes approvedLoggers[msg.sender] will fail when target != msg.sender (here msg.sender == address(this)).
        assertTrue(c.approvedLoggers(target) == status);
    }
}
